    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37550" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prae-dūro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. a.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i>to make very
			hard</i>, <i>harden very much</i> (postAug.):
			 sucus praeduratus, <i><span class="en">Plin. 23,
				7, 71, § 139</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Apic. 6,
			9</span></i>; <i><span class="en">7, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">8</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>to harden</i>, <i>indurate</i>, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 5, 177.</div>
